                <pb facs="0944" n="848" xml:id="pg848"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.51/89: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Schuyler</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-08-30T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 30,
                                1921—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>27. Department’s August 23, 6 P.M.</p>
                <p>Mr. Keith’s representative states that Mr. Keilhauer requests the good offices of
                    Department in obtaining an extension of the bank concession as well as the
                    option contract for the loan. You will therefore endeavor, by informal
                    representations, to procure from the President an extension of the bank contract
                    for 4 months, pointing out that the establishment of the bank necessarily
                    depends upon negotiations of the loan and that it will, therefore, be necessary
                    to delay the execution of both projects pending a decision from the American
                    bankers who have been approached.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
